Subject: [PATCH] drm/vkms: optimize NV12/ARGB composition and retain active consumers

Use portable bit scans for YUV fixed-point multiplication and precompute
8-bit NV12 channel contributions once before device registration. Keep
existing scaling, truncation, rounding, matrices and rotated chroma siting.
Dispatch XRGB8888 writeback once per row instead of indirectly per pixel.
Copy opaque pixels and skip zero transparent pixels with identical blending
semantics; retain the original equation for every other alpha/color value.
Skip the identity color-transform pass when no color pipeline is selected.
Tables occupy 108 KiB across six encoding/range pairs and become read-only
after module init. Other pixel formats retain their existing readers.
Fuse ARGB8888 expansion/blending without a color pipeline; read opaque NV12
straight into the output row. Keep CRC, geometry, alpha and color semantics.
Reference-count composer users so deferred writeback cleanup cannot disable
another writeback job or CRC capture. Initialize and queue writeback before
publishing wb_pending; read its job pointer under the same lock.
The composer reference operations adapt atipre's
"drm/vkms: Keep composition enabled for concurrent users" (2026-10-26):
https://go.mail-archive.com/dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org/msg646844.html
Skip ticks with neither pending writeback nor an active CRC reader. Keep the
ordered composer workqueue, using WQ_HIGHPRI for ordinary scheduling priority.
Baseline: Linux stable v7.3.3. Local experimental patch, not upstreamed.

